        "The Messenger of the Great Battles" to "Buyuk janglar xabarchisi",
        "Our Lord, accept this from us. Surely You are the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing." to "Robbimiz, buni bizdan qabul qil. Albatta, Sen eshitguvchi va bilguvchi zotsan.",
        "Our Lord, make us both submissive to You, and from our descendants a nation submissive to You. Show us our rites of worship and accept our repentance. Surely You are the Acceptor of repentance, the Most Merciful." to "Parvardigorimiz, bizni ikkimizni o‘zingga itoat qiluvchilardan qilgin, zurriyotlarimizdan esa o‘zingga itoatli ummat qilgin. Bizga ibodatlarimizni ko'rsat va tavbalarimizni qabul qil. Albatta, Sen tavbalarni qabul qiluvchi va rahmlisan.",
        "Our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and save us from the punishment of the Fire." to "Ey Robbimiz, bizga bu dunyoda ham, oxiratda ham yaxshilik bergin va bizni do'zax azobidan saqlagin.",
        "Our Lord, pour patience upon us, make our feet firm, and help us against the disbelieving people." to "Ey Robbimiz, ustimizdan sabr ber, oyoqlarimizni mustahkam qil va kofir qavmga qarshi bizga nusrat ber.",
        "Our Lord, do not take us to task if we forget or make a mistake." to "Robbimiz, agar unutsak yoki xato qilsak, bizni jazoga tortmagin.",
        "Our Lord, do not place on us a heavy burden like the one You placed on those before us." to "Ey Robbimiz, bizdan oldingilarga yuklaganingdek, bizga ham og'ir yuk yuklamagin.",
        "Our Lord, do not burden us with what we have no strength to bear. Pardon us, forgive us and have mercy on us. You are our Protector, so help us against the disbelieving people." to "Ey Robbimiz, bizni ko'tara olmaydigan narsani yuklama. Bizni kechir, bizni kechir va bizga rahm qil. Sen bizning valiymizsan, bas, kofir qavmga qarshi bizga yordam ber.",
        "Our Lord, do not let our hearts deviate after You have guided us, and grant us mercy from Yourself. Surely You are the Bestower." to "Ey Robbimiz, bizlarni hidoyat qilganingdan keyin qalblarimizni og'dirmagin va bizga O'z huzuringdan rahmat ato et. Albatta, Sen ato etguvchisan.",
        "Our Lord, You will surely gather all people on a Day about which there is no doubt. Surely Allah does not break His promise." to "Ey Robbimiz, Sen barcha odamlarni borligiga shak-shubhasiz Kunda jamlaysan. Albatta, Alloh va'dasiga xilof qilmaydi.",
        "Our Lord, we have believed, so forgive us our sins and save us from the punishment of the Fire." to "Ey Robbimiz, biz iymon keltirdik, gunohlarimizni mag‘firat qil va bizni do‘zax azobidan saqlagin.",
        "Our Lord, we believe in what You have revealed and we follow the Messenger, so write us among those who bear witness." to "Ey Robbimiz, biz nozil qilgan narsangga iymon keltirdik va Payg'ambarga ergashdik, bas, bizni guvohlik beruvchilardan yoz.",
        "Our Lord, forgive us our sins and our excesses in our affairs, make our feet firm, and help us against the disbelieving people." to "Ey Robbimiz, gunohlarimizni va ishimizdagi haddan oshganlarimizni mag'firat qil, oyoqlarimizni mustahkam qil va bizga kofir qavmlarga qarshi yordam ber.",
        "Our Lord, You have not created this without purpose. Glory be to You, so save us from the punishment of the Fire." to "Ey Robbimiz, Sen buni behuda yaratmading. Sen poksan, bizni do'zax azobidan saqla.",
        "Our Lord, whoever You admit to the Fire, You have surely disgraced him, and the wrongdoers have no helpers." to "Ey Robbimiz, kimni do'zaxga kiritsang, uni sharmanda qilding va zolimlarga yordamchi yo'qdir.",
        "Our Lord, we heard a caller calling to faith, saying: Believe in your Lord, so we believed." to "Ey Robbimiz, biz iymonga chorlovchining: «Robbingga iymon keltir, biz ham iymon keltirdik», deganini eshitdik.",
        "Our Lord, forgive us our sins, remove from us our misdeeds, and let us die with the righteous." to "Ey Robbimiz, gunohlarimizni mag‘firat qil, gunohlarimizni o‘chir va bizlarni solihlar bilan birga o‘ldir.",
        "Our Lord, grant us what You promised us through Your messengers, and do not disgrace us on the Day of Resurrection. Surely You do not break Your promise." to "Ey Robbimiz, bizga payg‘ambarlaring orqali va’da qilgan narsangni bergin va qiyomat kunida bizni sharmanda qilma. Albatta, Sen va'daingni buzmassan.",
        "Our Lord, we have believed, so write us among those who bear witness." to "Ey Robbimiz, biz iymon keltirdik, bas, bizni guvohlik beruvchilardan yoz.",
        "Our Lord, send down to us a table spread from heaven, to be a festival for the first of us and the last of us and a sign from You. Provide for us, for You are the best of providers." to "Ey Robbimiz, bizga osmondan yoyilgan dasturxonni tushirginki, birinchilarimizga ham, oxirgilarimizga ham bayram va O'zingdan oyat bo'lsin. Bizni rizqlantir, chunki Sen eng yaxshi rizq beruvchisan.",
        "Our Lord, we have wronged ourselves. If You do not forgive us and have mercy on us, we will surely be among the losers." to "Ey Robbimiz, biz o'zimizga zulm qildik. If You do not forgive us and have mercy on us, we will surely be among the losers.",
        "Our Lord, do not place us with the wrongdoing people." to "Ey Robbimiz, bizlarni zolim qavm bilan birga qilma.",
        "Our Lord, decide between us and our people with truth, for You are the best of those who decide." to "Ey Robbimiz, biz bilan qavmimiz oramizda haq ila hukm qil, chunki Sen hukm qilguvchilarning eng yaxshisisan.",
        "Our Lord, pour patience upon us and let us die as Muslims." to "Ey Robbimiz, bizlarga sabr bergin va bizlarni musulmon holida vafot et.",
        "Our Lord, do not make us a trial for the wrongdoing people, and save us by Your mercy from the disbelieving people." to "Ey Robbimiz, bizni zolim qavm uchun fitna qilma va bizni rahmating ila kofir qavmlardan qutqargin.",
        "Our Lord, You surely know what we conceal and what we reveal. Nothing on earth or in heaven is hidden from Allah." to "Ey Robbimiz, albatta, Sen bizning yashirganimizni ham, oshkor qilganimizni ham bilursan. Yerdagi va osmondagi hech narsa Allohga yashirin emas.",
        "My Lord, make me one who establishes prayer, and my descendants too. Our Lord, accept my supplication." to "Parvardigorim, meni ham, zurriyotimni ham namozni to‘kis ado etuvchi qilguvchi qilgin. Robbimiz, duolarimni qabul qil.",
        "Our Lord, forgive me, my parents and the believers on the Day when the reckoning is established." to "Robbimiz, meni, ota-onamni va mo'minlarni hisob-kitob qilinadigan kunda mag'firat qil.",
        "Our Lord, grant us mercy from Yourself and provide for us right guidance in our affair." to "Ey Robbimiz, bizga O'z huzuringdan rahmat ato et va ishimizda to'g'ri hidoyat bergin.",
        "Our Lord, we fear that he may hasten to harm us or that he may transgress." to "Ey Robbimiz, biz u bizga zarar yetkazishidan yoki haddan oshib ketishidan qo'rqamiz.",
        "Our Lord, we have believed, so forgive us and have mercy on us, for You are the best of the merciful." to "Ey Robbimiz, biz iymon keltirdik, bizlarni mag‘firat qil va bizga rahm qil, chunki Sen rahmlilarning eng yaxshisisan.",
        "Our Lord, turn away from us the punishment of Hell. Its punishment is truly unrelenting; it is indeed an evil abode and resting place." to "Ey Robbimiz, bizdan do'zax azobini qaytargin. Uning jazosi chindan ham shafqatsizdir; Albatta, u yomon joy va oromgohdir.",
        "Our Lord, grant us from our spouses and our children the coolness of our eyes, and make us leaders of the God-fearing." to "Parvardigorimiz, bizlarga juftlarimiz va farzandlarimizdan ko‘zlarimizga salqinlik ato et va bizlarni taqvodorlarning yetakchilaridan qil.",
        "Surely our Lord is All-Forgiving, Most Appreciative." to "Albatta, Robbimiz mag'firatli va shukr qilguvchidir.",
        "Our Lord, You encompass everything in mercy and knowledge, so forgive those who repent and follow Your path, and save them from the punishment of Hell." to "Ey Robbimiz, Sen hamma narsani rahmat va ilm bilan o'rab olgansan, bas, tavba qilib, Sening yo'lingga ergashganlarni mag'firat qil va ularni do'zax azobidan saqla.",
        "Our Lord, admit them to the Gardens of Eternity which You have promised them, along with the righteous among their parents, spouses and children. Surely You are the Almighty, the All-Wise. And protect them from evil deeds; whoever You protect from evil that Day, You have truly shown him mercy, and that is the supreme success." to "Ey Robbimiz, ularni ota-onalari, er-xotinlari va farzandlaridan solihlari bilan birga ularga va'da qilgan mangu jannatlarga kirit. Albatta, Sen aziz va hikmatli zotsan. Va ularni yomon ishlardan saqla. O'sha kunda kimni yomonlikdan saqlasang, albatta, unga rahm qilding va ana o'sha eng buyuk yutuqdir.",
        "Our Lord, forgive us and our brothers who preceded us in faith, and do not place in our hearts any ill-will towards those who believe." to "Ey Robbimiz, bizlarni va bizdan oldin iymonda o'tgan birodarlarimizni mag'firat qilgin va qalblarimizda iymon keltirgan zotlarga nisbatan yomonlikni qo'yma.",
        "Our Lord, surely You are Most Kind, Most Merciful." to "Robbimiz, albatta, Sen mehribon va rahmlisan.",
        "Our Lord, in You we put our trust, to You we turn, and to You is the final return." to "Ey Robbimiz, Senga tavakkul qildik, Senga tavba qildik va qaytish Sengadir.",
        "Our Lord, do not make us a trial for those who disbelieve, and forgive us, our Lord. Surely You are the Almighty, the All-Wise." to "Ey Robbimiz, bizni kufr keltirganlar uchun fitna qilmagin va bizlarni mag'firat qilgin, ey Robbimiz. Albatta, Sen aziz va hikmatli zotsan.",
        "Our Lord, perfect our light for us and forgive us. Surely You have power over all things." to "Ey Robbimiz, biz uchun nurimizni mukammal qil va bizlarni mag'firat qil. Albatta, Sen har narsaga qodirsan.",
        "Sahih al-Bukhari 2736, Sahih Muslim 2677" to "Sahih al-Buxoriy 2736, Sahihi Muslim 2677",
        "Sahih al-Bukhari 3532, Sahih Muslim 2354" to "Sahih al-Buxoriy 3532, Sahihi Muslim 2354",
        "The rak‘at below follow the Hanafi teaching. Fard is obligatory; Sunnah Muakkadah should not be left without an excuse; Sunnah Ghair-Muakkadah and Nafl are optional and rewarded." to "Quyidagi rak'at hanafiy ta'limotiga amal qiladi. Farz farzdir; Sunnat Muakkadani uzrsiz qoldirmaslik kerak; Sunnat g'ayri-muakkada va nafl ixtiyoriy va savobdir.",
        "In congregation the imam recites aloud in Fajr, in the first two rak‘at of Maghrib and Isha, and in Jumu‘ah and Eid. Zuhr and Asr are quiet. Praying alone, you may recite quietly in all of them." to "Imom bomdodda, shom va xuftonning birinchi ikki rakatida, juma va hayitda jamoat bilan ovoz chiqarib qiroat qiladi. Zuhr va asr tinch. Yolg'iz namoz o'qib, ularning barchasida jimgina o'qishingiz mumkin.",
        "Whoever prays twelve rak‘at of Sunnah in a day and night, a house is built for him in Paradise." to "Kim kechayu kunduz o'n ikki rakat sunnat namoz o'qisa, unga jannatda uy quriladi.",
        "Prayer times are on Home, and you can log your prayers in the Prayer tracker. This guide does not change your prayer-time calculation." to "Namoz vaqtlari Bosh sahifada va siz namozlaringizni Namoz kuzatuvchisida qayd etishingiz mumkin. Ushbu qo'llanma namoz vaqtini hisoblashingizni o'zgartirmaydi.",
        "This sequence of Sunnah and Nafl is the Hanafi teaching. Other schools may classify or arrange some of them differently." to "Sunnat va naflning bu ketma-ketligi hanafiy ta'limotidir. Boshqa maktablar ularning ba'zilarini boshqacha tarzda tasniflashi yoki tartibga solishlari mumkin.",
